  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The latest beta update seems to have silently added a new OSC endpoint `/avatar/name` that sends out the avatar's name.\n\nThis breaks when the avatar's name has complex UTF-8 characters. The characters seem to get truncated to a single byte, which most OSC applications cannot correctly decode.\n\nDebug menu \"Version & Info\": S:Release_1626 V:2026.4.1\n\nThis is extremely easy to reproduce with any avatar that has a `!` in its name, as that character gets transformed to U+01c3 on upload, which then gets truncated to a `c3` byte when sent over OSC, which cannot be decoded as valid UTF-8 (or ascii)\n\nThis is even more noticeable with avatars that contain Japanese character in their names.",
